1
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:18,460
Yesterday, I was online and I learned about a woman called Amy who walked all round the UK to get money for charity.

2
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:20,340
And in winter!

3
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:22,760
When there was rain and snow!

4
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:27,640
Do you know any other amazing stories like that?

5
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:31,100
How about Dee Caffari?

6
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:35,560
She sailed around the world, non-stop, three times!

7
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,320
That’s right, three times.

8
00:00:38,998 --> 00:00:41,060
Imagine the wind and the rain!

9
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:43,119
Fantastic, eh?

10
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:55,635
OK, well there’s a boy called Jordan Romero, from the US – he climbed Mount Everest when he was 13 years old.

11
00:00:56,260 --> 00:01:00,520
It’s really cold up there, but he managed to get to the top.

12
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:02,220
Only 13!

13
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:04,960
Now that’s an achievement.

14
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:14,080
My friend Corey Armstrong decided to run a marathon when he was 16.

15
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,507
He finished in just over four hours.

16
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:27,340
He enjoyed it a lot, so then he decided to do the marathon in Death Valley in the US.

17
00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:33,920
It’s so hot there – often more than 40 degrees Celsius.

18
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:42,900
This time he was slower, almost five hours – but I still think it’s fantastic.

19
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:48,320
42 kilometres when it’s over 40 degrees!

20
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:51,380
I think he almost died!

21
00:01:54,980 --> 00:02:06,630
Before 1926, a lot of women tried to swim the cold water of the English Channel from England to France – but they all failed.

22
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:20,920
But in 1926, Gertrude Ederle (an Olympic gold medal swimmer) arrived on an English beach after 14 hours and 31 minutes.

23
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:25,700
She returned to her home in New York a hero!

24
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:27,780
How about that!?

